      "published": "2026-11-24T16:11:52Z",
      "score": 25,
      "comments": 1,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50630294",
      "snippet": "Hi HN! TLDR: we’ve built an open-source drop-in replacement for a postgres read-replica, powered by duckdb’s columnar compute engine. It’s very fast. And it looks like postgres.<p>So, this started out as: let’s just connect Clickhouse to our postgres dbs and throw our analytics queries at it instead. That will speed everything up.  But we quickly found that 1) Clickhouse comes with quite the learning curve (engine optimisation) to make it fast (we needed something we could easily drop in to any customer’s postgres scenario), and 2) we had underestimated how different clickhouse’s SQL syntax was to postgres.  Don’t get me wrong: we love Clickhouse (it’s ridiculously fast if you know what queries to expect), it just didn’t work for our ad-hoc postgres workloads.<p>So we went searching for alternatives that were 1) more plug-and-play and 2) looked a lot more like postgres.<p>We dismissed a ",
